\ S6d probe K — the (Some, Some) different-root join refusal must keep
\ happening (desk-check A.iii; Ruling F / SOO-41 territory at the join). Two
\ views of two DIFFERENT frame locals are bound before the branch; each arm
\ packs its own view into the Step slot, so the join sees two rooted derivs
\ with different `owned_root`s and refuses rather than picking one arm's
\ root. Clean tree: no impl, no fence — the join rule fires as-is, the pin.
import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;
import: hosted::show | . | ;

type: Step['T 'Rest]
| Done
| More 'T 'Rest
;

: main ( -- )
  3 1 fill |a| 4 1 fill |b|
  &a slice |va| &b slice |vb|
  True
  ~[ vb 7 swap More ]
  ~[ va 8 swap More ]
  if
  ~[ ( Done ) drop ] ~[ ( More ) More> drop drop ] Step?
  a drop b drop ;
